#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175619 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "2f4571af-99cf-5a4a-9998-fb6a0f7d6be9" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-11004" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\tan x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n1. The zeros of the function are at $x = \\pi n$.\n2. The function has asymptotes at $x = 2\\pi n$.\n3. The range of the function is $y\\in [-1,1]$." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3558/Source/Images/8b2ecc027eb04e0cb4a12ecd0b0191cf.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The zeros occur at $x=0, \\pm \\pi, \\pm2\\pi,\\ldots$, which can be written as $x=n\\pi$.\n- Statement II is false. The function has an asymptote at $x = \\dfrac \\pi 2$ and the period is $\\pi$. Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x = \\dfrac \\pi 2 + \\pi n$.\n- Statement III is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $y\\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175620 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eed0c7c3-0bb5-56eb-a9ca-9ec4dc7b3efe" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "f4649856-d777-5468-a7f4-df50479e36d7" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-11005" :question/problem "If $\\tan\\left(x\\right) = -2$ for some value of $x$, then find the value of $\\tan\\left(x-2\\pi\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\tan x$ is $\\pi$. Therefore, for any integer $n$, we have\n\n$$\n\\tan x = \\tan (x+n\\pi)\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\tan x &= \\tan (x + (-2) \\cdot π) = \\tan (x - 2π)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\tan\\left(x\\right) = -2\n$$\n\nwe get that\n\n$$\n\\tan\\left(x-2\\pi\\right) = -2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175628 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66a1733a-d7bb-5c86-a154-9e54422053a7" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "0b146642-914c-52ce-9939-86752e95dcd2" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-11013" :question/problem "If $\\tan x = -\\dfrac{2}{3}$, find the value of $\\tan (-x+7\\pi)$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\tan{x}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3558/Source/Images/d01abb298d92d64b71126490ab06b4ed.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $\\tan{x}$ is $\\pi$.\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $\\tan{x}$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n$\\tan(-x) = -\\tan{x}$.\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $\\tan{x}$, we have\n$\\tan (-x + 7π)|= \\tan (-x + π \\cdot 7); = \\tan (-x)$.\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $\\tan{x}$, we have\n$\\tan (-x)|=-\\tan x; = - (-\\frac{2}{3})$.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\tan (-x+7\\pi)=\\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44e70e67-040e-58ec-8e2b-2215930016dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246712} {:answer/id #uuid "c39ea976-b5f9-5004-a552-68c5c025132b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246713} {:answer/id #uuid "961ce003-6035-5a1f-9aa6-141fd94606dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246714} {:answer/id #uuid "749bbc90-2eb3-5bf8-94a4-e98f5302c1c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246715} {:answer/id #uuid "b08c447a-cc1d-58c7-87af-7e3ac3d32a74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "961ce003-6035-5a1f-9aa6-141fd94606dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246714} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3944d1c-16bd-589e-b90e-443fdf8f4cd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246711}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "264dc1d8-6c35-583a-b855-2ee23edf3c8d" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-103289" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $\n- The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n$\n- The range of the function is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/732955302ca49a41f6c43cf242d7c869e630e88d804c4b56a5beb3b081f2d230.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is defined everywhere, except where $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246717 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e88fdd70-1af2-5d17-af59-4f2afd8ef738" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246719} {:answer/id #uuid "22d203ee-ab5a-5dfb-8879-4e89e5cf102d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246720} {:answer/id #uuid "3ab27600-9377-5b2b-a4b4-dc6697afd59c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246721} {:answer/id #uuid "6adf4eaa-a986-5f83-911e-4759f7bd183f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246722} {:answer/id #uuid "6e945b93-d364-508a-92fa-2823a1c5dbe4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e88fdd70-1af2-5d17-af59-4f2afd8ef738" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246719} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8979ad8-23a5-583c-b1b2-f6796537e051" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246718}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "317d2b9c-f42d-5ece-9543-51e9cfb75b9f" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-103295" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\n- The vertical asymptotes of the function are $x=2n\\pi $\n- Its graph passes through the point $(0,0)$\n- $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=tan⁡(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6})$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/c2d0606829588b01f6cba2fa4785b201c47a6d9ffa325d54e64544c9769d7e4a.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the graph of the function passes through the point $(0,0).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi )=tan⁡(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6}).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246724 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eed0c7c3-0bb5-56eb-a9ca-9ec4dc7b3efe" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8c6e9d2-f837-595b-b2ab-6e30e5afe2e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246726} {:answer/id #uuid "c474b438-f75e-5326-b86f-ea37380b08b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246727} {:answer/id #uuid "df77ed1e-085a-511f-b92a-5085944e2627" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246728} {:answer/id #uuid "077336e3-2026-52ac-8db5-9ea4440b56ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246729} {:answer/id #uuid "e0bb8569-0e94-501e-a382-2594d35f01cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0bb8569-0e94-501e-a382-2594d35f01cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246730} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0e1aa4d-b0f0-5fdd-8985-76afd50887a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246725}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86a6763e-11cd-57bc-8cd3-73cb100b14e0" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-103307" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=\\frac{1}{3},$ for some value of $x,$ find the value of $12tan⁡(x+5\\pi )-6.$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡x=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡x=tan⁡(x+5\\cdot \\pi )=tan⁡(x+5\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $tan⁡x=\\frac{1}{3},$ we get that $tan⁡(x+5\\pi )=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n12tan⁡(x+5\\pi )-6=12(\\frac{1}{3})-6=4-6=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246731 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eed0c7c3-0bb5-56eb-a9ca-9ec4dc7b3efe" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbb42df1-0b63-574a-ad4d-193e63df65ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12+\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246733} {:answer/id #uuid "e0a826f0-a3c2-575e-989c-e86c586003a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246734} {:answer/id #uuid "a0940e30-9ec3-5128-8c82-e880d846d564" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12-3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246735} {:answer/id #uuid "62a56e7e-f263-5601-9c41-6d5e7130a087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246736} {:answer/id #uuid "5995d2fa-428e-55e4-a841-d5291f482148" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0a826f0-a3c2-575e-989c-e86c586003a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246734} :answer-field/id #uuid "29f20fba-52a1-5c6d-9240-70e34c955fa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246732}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "95a5187e-80fa-5229-bf10-a6677dad6740" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-103312" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=16,$ for some value of $x,$ find the value of $\\frac{3}{4}tan⁡(x-9\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡x=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-9$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡x=tan⁡(x+(-9)\\cdot \\pi )=tan⁡(x-9\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $tan⁡x=16,$ we get that $tan⁡(x-9\\pi )=16.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}tan⁡(x-9\\pi )=\\frac{3}{4}(16)=12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66a1733a-d7bb-5c86-a154-9e54422053a7" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3a94382-6334-5d6e-b5ba-42e4999251d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174277} {:answer/id #uuid "cafcc4e9-a02b-55d7-aaaa-ed8952cc5efb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174278} {:answer/id #uuid "cdaaa308-e9e5-5c23-a80b-cffbaa339154" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174279} {:answer/id #uuid "5894476c-02e6-5f0b-adf2-f1af972e7a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174280} {:answer/id #uuid "6018e45d-a275-5ed6-b668-e5ef2a26402b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3a94382-6334-5d6e-b5ba-42e4999251d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174277} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d9c5fac-2ff8-5b25-91eb-1cc1a80648d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174276}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ccd7ae50-1c4e-5bcc-8b8b-d405f5154f0b" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-136548" :question/problem "If $\\tan a =-2$, then $\\tan (-a) =$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nOur graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{∘}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-a) & =-tan⁡a \\\\  & =-(-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246738 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66a1733a-d7bb-5c86-a154-9e54422053a7" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "935ecc4c-8ed9-58a8-b9e3-63ecd9876944" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246740} {:answer/id #uuid "541e6025-9a73-5759-aec0-5ed3af101226" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246741} {:answer/id #uuid "fa80783e-f589-5967-8cf1-4db5ba5c97f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246742} {:answer/id #uuid "fc71bbe2-b118-557c-8d4c-d24bf0b90666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246743} {:answer/id #uuid "816e425e-95f6-5f3b-abf8-7976bd7ce287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "935ecc4c-8ed9-58a8-b9e3-63ecd9876944" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246740} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9cef918-b950-5e90-b859-43893bf093ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246739}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43f38354-d453-5a54-bedd-c97200da2de6" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-136639" :question/problem "If $tan⁡a=\\frac{4}{5},$ then $tan⁡(-a)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nOur graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{∘}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-a) & =-tan⁡a \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246745 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66a1733a-d7bb-5c86-a154-9e54422053a7" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fa05a7d-837f-5014-ab4b-481dce1ee09f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246747} {:answer/id #uuid "2d3ed6f8-2111-582e-a331-1efe7961e0cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246748} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad6eab1-520d-5c88-bb91-967a68010b17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246749} {:answer/id #uuid "07ce8ac1-c336-5e8e-be6e-50e7017a127a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246750} {:answer/id #uuid "053cecc9-7f20-53ff-9e9a-94dce16ff772" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ad6eab1-520d-5c88-bb91-967a68010b17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246749} :answer-field/id #uuid "82a3a743-9913-5a6b-9c7e-e286e475eec0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246746}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "45df303f-70b4-57c7-8eeb-36e8cb5c5cfb" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-158038" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=3,$ then $tan⁡(-x)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nOur graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{∘}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x) & =-tan⁡x \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66a1733a-d7bb-5c86-a154-9e54422053a7" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0091aa30-09bf-5a3f-9b92-18ff012af49d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246754} {:answer/id #uuid "2fe09367-8d58-5cdb-931e-810c1b9b1988" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246755} {:answer/id #uuid "6aa2314b-8077-5f5e-aaa8-24f8fe179acb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246756} {:answer/id #uuid "8a139043-4a92-5b9a-b86c-7c070005be47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246757} {:answer/id #uuid "f9c374c9-b095-5e2c-bc39-0efbed8aa6c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9c374c9-b095-5e2c-bc39-0efbed8aa6c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246758} :answer-field/id #uuid "37b92d9e-62b7-5ad8-891c-381fd78cc8b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246753}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6beda82e-a20a-5d58-a4e3-3ff246d0aab0" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-158041" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=-4,$ then $\\frac{1}{2}tan⁡(-x+3\\pi )+3=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x+3\\pi ) & =tan⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x) & =-tan⁡x \\\\  & =-(-4) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}tan⁡(-x+3\\pi )+3 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4+3 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2}+3 \\\\  & =2+3 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66a1733a-d7bb-5c86-a154-9e54422053a7" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Oddness Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f4b4477-660e-5714-b505-d0a25a2344b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246761} {:answer/id #uuid "c1e6cf9f-c1ae-5769-a71d-df1788898d95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246762} {:answer/id #uuid "8dace757-b9ec-56f2-9400-1269df92064b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246763} {:answer/id #uuid "9e9d5c41-1c3c-5f72-aed0-00655708ae51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246764} {:answer/id #uuid "157f0816-893e-5932-b514-0192d3b68646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dace757-b9ec-56f2-9400-1269df92064b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246763} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a16fdac-8762-505c-a542-af7c74cd4100" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246760}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e8566090-d643-5dbe-8765-e92369416700" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-158046" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=-2,$ then $\\frac{3}{5}tan⁡(-x-7\\pi )+\\frac{4}{5}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x-7\\pi ) & =tan⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x) & =-tan⁡x \\\\  & =-(-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}tan⁡(-x-7\\pi )+\\frac{4}{5} & =\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot 2+\\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}+\\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85f53242-b161-5061-b2e6-21454c0aa47a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174801} {:answer/id #uuid "dc875309-87cf-5386-8c20-9cac6e4c3c23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174802} {:answer/id #uuid "ee521ecc-bde5-51e0-a9c7-9fa0450ac9b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174803} {:answer/id #uuid "4505287a-b44e-5953-bdfd-6fc4749e3020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174804} {:answer/id #uuid "647bb7e7-374a-5350-8015-2a7421e5c3a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4505287a-b44e-5953-bdfd-6fc4749e3020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174804} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ee3205f-bac2-5d75-a8b4-6c10b6d8d2e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174800}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ac898e3a-bbc1-536e-8415-2d3fbc798e28" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-27638" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\tan x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n1. The function has asymptotes at $x = nπ$.\n2. The function returns only positive values on the intervals $(πn, \\frac{π}{2} + πn)$.\n3. The function has zeros at $x = \\frac{π}{2} + nπ$." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/326418398ce1a33f03a21f3bdb58107856f4ccb72241429f1604486281e60822.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function returns only positive values on the interval $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the function is positive on $(n\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi )\\,.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246766 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57c8061b-6304-50f4-8639-49df6546865a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246768} {:answer/id #uuid "99e13b58-77bb-5f71-afc8-21d1feaa855f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246769} {:answer/id #uuid "0f3efb74-8a3d-5cad-82a2-9d3e8b0b8d89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246770} {:answer/id #uuid "134ed3a0-8b4e-57f7-b6d8-9846c0144eb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246771} {:answer/id #uuid "6a83dd0b-504f-5ddd-b816-f900a2db858a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99e13b58-77bb-5f71-afc8-21d1feaa855f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246769} :answer-field/id #uuid "e838b5c5-420a-5bb5-ae26-c4d18b43ae16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246767}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a50a54b2-642a-5810-b035-b477949523f0" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-28675" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\n- $tan⁡(x+\\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).$\n- The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi $\n- $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=tan⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/31b430f003171dcc04a8f17402d6035fbbc305c244d3676bbf5da83fa447bd50.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x+\\pi )=tan⁡(x)=tan⁡(x+n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi )=tan⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246773 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a052a079-715a-50a6-810b-0672caede357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246775} {:answer/id #uuid "187883db-7955-5ba8-acd5-afc1c014a35b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246776} {:answer/id #uuid "2ddfd7ce-95fd-515f-b2e3-7163e700eb36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246777} {:answer/id #uuid "b17045a2-633d-548c-bcae-239dc7f561a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246778} {:answer/id #uuid "e313fd4f-5890-5bfc-bdb5-c0c87715a5d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e313fd4f-5890-5bfc-bdb5-c0c87715a5d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246779} :answer-field/id #uuid "31b8fc33-67bf-512c-a450-8f06bb931f2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246774}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "22cad6db-7a8e-526c-ae29-9691aa02e418" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-29608" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\n- The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi .$\n- $tan⁡(x)=tan⁡(x+2n\\pi ).$\n- The range of the function is $[-1,1].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/31b430f003171dcc04a8f17402d6035fbbc305c244d3676bbf5da83fa447bd50.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x+2n\\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\\pi +n\\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\\pi )=tan⁡(x).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The range of $y=tan⁡x$ is $(-\\infty ,+\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eed0c7c3-0bb5-56eb-a9ca-9ec4dc7b3efe" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0709f4b1-7585-54fe-9e9b-2d0f09ab6984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246782} {:answer/id #uuid "9d679a39-e7bb-5803-8ec7-f3c27b79741e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246783} {:answer/id #uuid "83e546ba-c6f0-5ef6-89ca-ce20d8a4f310" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}+2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246784} {:answer/id #uuid "c66eda7e-133a-5408-a3e3-fc21be6e02f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246785} {:answer/id #uuid "bce17e77-dd47-550d-b4d6-b5d1f62f3fea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0709f4b1-7585-54fe-9e9b-2d0f09ab6984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246782} :answer-field/id #uuid "26637c84-2699-5d35-8fcd-103420876747" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246781}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "022c6c58-a2d3-57ca-999d-54e67f40fd2a" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-66594" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=\\sqrt{3},$ for some $x$, find the value of $tan⁡(x-5\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡x=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-5$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡x=tan⁡(x+(-5)\\cdot \\pi )=tan⁡(x-5\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $tan⁡x=\\sqrt{3},$ we get that $tan⁡(x-5\\pi )=\\sqrt{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eed0c7c3-0bb5-56eb-a9ca-9ec4dc7b3efe" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0bb51a4-37b4-5012-aebc-26f7dca082a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246789} {:answer/id #uuid "2f3c2a7d-d53e-53f5-aa7e-30ddc1281d5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246790} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d0d44b-aa48-517d-9e17-4e3f0eda5846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246791} {:answer/id #uuid "09290c50-7d58-5923-9413-31a0976cd14b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246792} {:answer/id #uuid "0bdaa1a6-0ad9-5cbf-b467-296fec6d9591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bdaa1a6-0ad9-5cbf-b467-296fec6d9591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246793} :answer-field/id #uuid "0176d211-23d8-5a42-be58-b80d0af775e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246788}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7545925d-7dfd-5d24-a762-651c6dabc4dc" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-70998" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=3,$ for some $x$, find the value of $tan⁡(x+5\\pi )+2.$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡x=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡x=tan⁡(x+5\\cdot \\pi )=tan⁡(x+5\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $tan⁡x=3,$ we get that $tan⁡(x+5\\pi )=3.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\ntan⁡(x+5\\pi )+2=(3)+2=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186246794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eed0c7c3-0bb5-56eb-a9ca-9ec4dc7b3efe" :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c9b6bfc-de31-597d-90c3-3de620d79bd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246796} {:answer/id #uuid "82cda237-cedf-558d-af58-25266e16adf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-11\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246797} {:answer/id #uuid "9b414b61-e3ed-5c48-a0b2-b0617825db1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246798} {:answer/id #uuid "6b92008b-543e-5669-a0b9-caa861721588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246799} {:answer/id #uuid "5b535575-7518-51a2-b28a-7d1b4485a6bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c9b6bfc-de31-597d-90c3-3de620d79bd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246796} :answer-field/id #uuid "77680353-3c42-558d-a61f-8f195d58b256" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246795}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "907d5d54-e887-533c-8a1d-6502c5fe59f2" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-71002" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=\\sqrt{2},$ for some $x$, find the value of $tan⁡(x-11\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡x=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-11$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡x=tan⁡(x+(-11)\\cdot \\pi )=tan⁡(x-11\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $tan⁡x=\\sqrt{2},$ we get that $tan⁡(x-11\\pi )=\\sqrt{2}.$"}]}
